label Day2
# story entry day=2
# art scene draft.reading.early
\Lavinia closes the door on the music from the bar. Her coat goes over the back of the chair. #id:line.Day2.one
\She sits at the corner of the table, close enough that one menu will do. #id:line.Day2.002
\Her fingers brush the cuff of my right sleeve before she opens the card. #id:line.Day2.003
\“Still damp.” #id:line.Day2.004
\“A little.” #id:line.Day2.005
\“You should have taken your coat off.” #id:line.Day2.006
\“I'm fine.” #id:line.Day2.007
\She looks down at the menu. #id:line.Day2.008
\“I thought you were only staying for a drink.” #id:line.Day2.009
\“Have you eaten?” #id:line.Day2.010
\“No.” #id:line.Day2.011
\“Then choose something.” #id:line.Day2.012
\“Do you want dinner?” #id:line.Day2.013
\“I was hoping to.” #id:line.Day2.014
\“The mushroom tart.” #id:line.Day2.015
\Lavinia turns the page. #id:line.Day2.016
\“Or the chicken.” #id:line.Day2.017
\The page comes back. Her finger finds the tart again. #id:line.Day2.018
\“I'll have the chicken.” #id:line.Day2.019
\“You don't have to.” #id:line.Day2.020
\“I want to try it.” #id:line.Day2.021
\“So do I.” #id:line.Day2.022
\“I noticed.” #id:line.Day2.023
\After we order, she rests her elbows on the table. #id:line.Day2.024
\“You can relax.” #id:line.Day2.025
\The shoulders settle against the chair. A little farther down; the edge of the table rises toward the chin. #id:line.Day2.026
\“Not that much.” #id:line.Day2.027
\“You're difficult to please.” #id:line.Day2.028
\“You haven't tried very hard.” #id:line.Day2.029
\Another inch. The chair creaks. #id:line.Day2.030
\Lavinia laughs and catches my wrist. #id:line.Day2.031
\“Come back.” #id:line.Day2.032
\I sit up. Her fingers remain around the wrist until the food arrives. #id:line.Day2.033
\For a while, we eat. She pushes her plate toward me. #id:line.Day2.034
\“Try that.” #id:line.Day2.035
# self-talk
\I could ask her to feed me. #id:line.Day2.036
label Day2.thought
# story marker {"kind":"thought.pass","payload":{"opportunity_id":"Day2.food","yes_target_id":"target.Day2.food.yes","pass_target_id":"target.Day2.food.default"}}
return

label Day2.food.yes
# story entry day=2
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“Give me a bite.” #id:line.Day2.food.yes.001
\“You have a fork.” #id:line.Day2.food.yes.002
\“I know.” #id:line.Day2.food.yes.003
\Lavinia cuts a smaller piece from the tart. #id:line.Day2.food.yes.004
\“Come here, then.” #id:line.Day2.food.yes.005
\I lean forward. She holds the fork still. #id:line.Day2.food.yes.006
\“Careful. It's hot.” #id:line.Day2.food.yes.007
\When I sit back, she pushes the plate into the space between us. #id:line.Day2.food.yes.008
\“Now eat your own.” #id:line.Day2.food.yes.009
label Day2.food.yes.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day2.answer"}}
return

label Day2.food.default
# story entry day=2
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“I should have ordered yours.” #id:line.Day2.food.default.001
\“You're eating it.” #id:line.Day2.food.default.002
\I take another piece before she draws the plate back. #id:line.Day2.food.default.003
\“Some of it.” #id:line.Day2.food.default.004
\She leaves it between us. #id:line.Day2.food.default.005
label Day2.food.default.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day2.answer"}}
return

label Day2.answer
# story entry day=2
# art scene draft.reading.early
# story challenge {"challenge_id":"Day2.challenge","playable_marker_id":"Day2.answer.playable","end_marker_id":"Day2.answer.end","board_profile_id":"week.canonical_solo","targets":{"never_started":"target.Day2.result.A","unfinished":"target.Day2.result.B","won":"target.Day2.result.C","lost":"target.Day2.result.D","perfect":"target.Day2.result.E"}}
\Her elbow stays on the corner of the wood. #id:line.Day2.answer.001
\“What?” I ask. #id:line.Day2.answer.002
\“I told you yesterday not to look too pleased.” #id:line.Day2.answer.003
\“This is my ordinary face.” #id:line.Day2.answer.004
\“It isn't.” #id:line.Day2.answer.005
\Her thumb touches the corner of my mouth, takes a flake of pastry from the skin, and returns to her glass. #id:line.Day2.answer.006
\“I could take you out tomorrow.” #id:line.Day2.answer.007
\“You could let me finish this.” #id:line.Day2.answer.008
\“The day after, then.” #id:line.Day2.answer.009
\Lavinia puts her fork down. #id:line.Day2.answer.010
\“Who had all this while I was away?” #id:line.Day2.answer.011
\“You aren't away now.” #id:line.Day2.answer.012
\Her hand opens between the plates. I put mine into it. #id:line.Day2.answer.013
\The thumb passes over one knuckle, then rests. #id:line.Day2.answer.014
\“Did you want me to stay?” #id:line.Day2.answer.015
\“You are staying.” #id:line.Day2.answer.016
\“Before I went.” #id:line.Day2.answer.017
\The edge of the plate against my wrist. Her hand still open beneath mine. #id:line.Day2.answer.018
\I could tell her I wanted her to stay. #id:line.Day2.answer.019
label Day2.answer.playable
# story marker {"kind":"challenge.playable","payload":{"challenge_id":"Day2.challenge"}}
label Day2.answer.end
# story marker {"kind":"challenge.end","payload":{"challenge_id":"Day2.challenge"}}
return

label Day2.result.A
# story entry day=2
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“Of course I did.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.001
\“Then why do I have to ask?” #id:line.Day2.result.A.002
\“I wanted you here, Lavinia.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.003
\Her thumb passes over the knuckle once more. #id:line.Day2.result.A.004
\“I asked you to check the English.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.005
\“You'd left a line out.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.006
\The hand slips out from under mine. #id:line.Day2.result.A.007
\“I'm not giving you anything else to send.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.008
\“I could still look at it.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.009
\“No.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.010
\“The wording wasn't—” #id:line.Day2.result.A.011
\“No.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.012
\I pick up my glass. She waits until I put it down. #id:line.Day2.result.A.013
\“All right.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.014
\Lavinia returns to her food. For a while there is only the cutlery and the music through the door. #id:line.Day2.result.A.015
\I push my plate toward her. #id:line.Day2.result.A.016
\“Was that the last piece?” #id:line.Day2.result.A.017
\“No.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.018
\She takes it. #id:line.Day2.result.A.019
\When she has finished, she puts her fork down beside the knife. #id:line.Day2.result.A.020
\“I should go.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.021
\“I could walk with you.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.022
\“I want to go on my own.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.023
\I draw my chair in so she can get past. #id:line.Day2.result.A.024
\At the door she stops to put on her coat. #id:line.Day2.result.A.025
\“Tell me when you get home.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.026
\“No. You'll ask whether I'm going to bed.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.027
\“Will you be?” #id:line.Day2.result.A.028
\“There.” #id:line.Day2.result.A.029
\She opens the door before I can answer. #id:line.Day2.result.A.030
\At my desk, I open the conversation. Good night. I add her name and send it. The lamp is still on when I put the phone down. #id:line.Day2.result.A.031
label Day2.result.A.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day3"}}
return

label Day2.result.B
# story entry day=2
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“I don't want to start that tonight.” #id:line.Day2.result.B.001
\“I'm asking about you.” #id:line.Day2.result.B.002
\“I know.” #id:line.Day2.result.B.003
\Her hand stays open beneath mine. #id:line.Day2.result.B.004
\“Then?” #id:line.Day2.result.B.005
\I turn my hand over and set it beside the plate. #id:line.Day2.result.B.006
\Lavinia folds her fingers into her palm. #id:line.Day2.result.B.007
\The edge of the menu has gone soft where it touches the wet glass. #id:line.Day2.result.B.008
\“Stay until we've finished eating.” #id:line.Day2.result.B.009
\Lavinia draws her plate toward her. #id:line.Day2.result.B.010
\She eats the last piece without offering it. I take a drink. #id:line.Day2.result.B.011
\When I put the glass down, she has her coat over her arm. #id:line.Day2.result.B.012
\“Lavinia.” #id:line.Day2.result.B.013
\She waits. #id:line.Day2.result.B.014
\The folded menu is still between the glasses. #id:line.Day2.result.B.015
\“Nothing.” #id:line.Day2.result.B.016
\She leaves. #id:line.Day2.result.B.017
\The conversation is open at my desk. About what you asked. I leave the words there while I take off my watch. When I pick up the phone again, I remove them and close the conversation. #id:line.Day2.result.B.018
label Day2.result.B.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day3"}}
return

label Day2.result.C
# story entry day=2
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“Yes. I wanted you here.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.001
\“And you decided I should be.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.002
\“I wanted it to be possible.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.003
\“You knew what I wanted.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.004
\“Yes.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.005
\Lavinia begins to draw her hand away. I open mine. #id:line.Day2.result.C.006
\She rests her hand beside the plate. #id:line.Day2.result.C.007
\“I'm not giving you anything else to send.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.008
\“All right.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.009
\“You'd still want to change it.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.010
\“Probably.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.011
\“Priscilla.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.012
\“I'm not asking for it.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.013
\She turns her glass. I wait until she has taken a drink. #id:line.Day2.result.C.014
\Lavinia reaches behind her for the coat. #id:line.Day2.result.C.015
\“Stay a little longer.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.016
\“Doing what?” #id:line.Day2.result.C.017
\“Having dinner with me.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.018
\“We've been doing that.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.019
\“I like it.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.020
\For a moment she holds the glass against her lower lip. #id:line.Day2.result.C.021
\Then she puts it down. #id:line.Day2.result.C.022
\“Until we finish.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.023
\Her hand leaves the coat. #id:line.Day2.result.C.024
\I cut another piece of chicken. #id:line.Day2.result.C.025
\Lavinia watches the knife come down again. #id:line.Day2.result.C.026
\“That's small enough.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.027
\“Is it?” #id:line.Day2.result.C.028
\“Eat it.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.029
\I do. She moves her chair closer to reach my plate and takes the other piece. #id:line.Day2.result.C.030
\For a while, neither of us says anything. #id:line.Day2.result.C.031
\When the plates are empty, she reaches for her coat. I stay in my chair. #id:line.Day2.result.C.032
\“Tell me when you get home.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.033
\“I will.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.034
\She rests her hand on my shoulder while she puts her coat on. I turn toward it. #id:line.Day2.result.C.035
\The pressure lifts. #id:line.Day2.result.C.036
\“Good night, Priscilla.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.037
\“Good night.” #id:line.Day2.result.C.038
\At my desk, the phone lights. #id:line.Day2.result.C.039
\Lavinia, message\: Home. #id:line.Day2.result.C.040
\Priscilla, message\: Good night, Lavinia. #id:line.Day2.result.C.041
\I leave the conversation open while I turn off the lamp. #id:line.Day2.result.C.042
label Day2.result.C.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day3"}}
return

