label Day2.result.D
# story entry day=2
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“Did you want me to stay?” #id:line.Day2.result.D.001
\“Yes.” #id:line.Day2.result.D.002
\Her thumb does not move. #id:line.Day2.result.D.003
\“I wanted you here.” #id:line.Day2.result.D.004
\“I asked you to check the English.” #id:line.Day2.result.D.005
\“You'd left a line out.” #id:line.Day2.result.D.006
\“On purpose.” #id:line.Day2.result.D.007
\“I know.” #id:line.Day2.result.D.008
\Lavinia takes her hand away. #id:line.Day2.result.D.009
\“Would you do it again?” #id:line.Day2.result.D.010
\“I'd show you first.” #id:line.Day2.result.D.011
\“And if I told you not to send it?” #id:line.Day2.result.D.012
\“Then I wouldn't send it.” #id:line.Day2.result.D.013
\“You mean that?” #id:line.Day2.result.D.014
\“If you don't want me to.” #id:line.Day2.result.D.015
\She turns the glass by its stem. A wet crescent remains on the table. #id:line.Day2.result.D.016
\“You'd find something else.” #id:line.Day2.result.D.017
\“You wouldn't have stopped on your own.” #id:line.Day2.result.D.018
